1. Definitions

"Copyright Holder" means the person identified in the copyright notice above,
but only to the extent that person owns or is authorized to license the rights
in question.

"Software" means the ViiOS source code, executable code, documentation, assets,
and other material that the Copyright Holder expressly supplies under this
license, including protected portions of that material. Independently licensed
third-party material is governed by Section 10.

"You" means the individual exercising rights under this license in their own
capacity. This license does not grant an organization a shared or institutional
license. Organizational deployment requires separate written permission.

"Third Party" means any person or legal entity other than You or the Copyright
Holder. Family members, colleagues, employers, clients, affiliated entities,
students, and other members of a group are Third Parties.

"Use" means to download, inspect, reproduce, install, compile, execute, or
otherwise operate the Software. Use does not include a right to Distribute.

"Modify" means to edit, adapt, translate, alter, or combine the Software with
other material to create a Derivative Work. Permission to Modify is separate
from, and does not imply, permission to Distribute.

"Derivative Work" means a modified version or other work incorporating or
adapting protectable expression from the Software. Merely interoperating with
the Software does not, by itself, make independently created work a Derivative
Work. The service restrictions in Section 4 apply regardless of this distinction.

"Distribute" means to give, transmit, publish, upload, supply, sell, rent, lend,
license, sublicense, transfer, or otherwise make the Software or a Derivative
Work available to a Third Party, in source, executable, archive, container,
embedded, or other form. This includes patches containing protected Software
material and making a repository or download accessible to a Third Party,
whether publicly or privately, directly or through an intermediary.

"Commercial Use" means Use directed toward or materially supporting revenue,
compensation, profit, commercial advantage, or business operations, whether
directly or indirectly. It includes Use in a for-profit organization's internal
operations, employee work for that organization, client work, paid consulting,
commercial product development or evaluation, and paid or revenue-supported
products or services. Neither lack of resale nor absence of a separate charge
for the Software makes such Use noncommercial.

"Noncommercial Use" means Use that is not Commercial Use. Education, research,
testing, hobby activity, and nonprofit status are not automatic exemptions:
the actual purpose and circumstances must satisfy this definition and all
other conditions of this license.

"Personal Use" means Use by You, for Your own purposes and without providing
the Software or its functionality to a Third Party. Personal Use is permitted
only when it is also Noncommercial Use; running a business on a personal
computer is not permitted Personal Use.

"Private Environment" means computers, storage, and servers under Your control
where the Software, Derivative Works, and their functionality are accessible
only to You. A personal remote server may qualify; a shared team deployment,
public endpoint, or third-party-accessible repository does not. This license
does not authorize giving a hosting or other service provider rights in, or
access to, the Software beyond independently existing rights in Section 10.

2. Limited copyright permission

Subject to every applicable condition of this license, the Copyright Holder
grants You a worldwide, royalty-free, nonexclusive, nontransferable, and
nonsublicensable copyright license to obtain an authorized copy, inspect its
source, make private working and backup copies, install, compile, execute, and
Modify the Software solely for Your own Noncommercial Use in a Private
Environment. This includes personal learning, independent noncommercial
research, private testing, and hobbies that satisfy those conditions.

You may keep a local version-control repository. You may run Your modified
version privately. Neither action authorizes sharing it. All rights not
expressly granted are reserved by the Copyright Holder. No ownership is sold
or transferred, and no further permission arises from availability of source.

3. No distribution or transfer

You must not Distribute the original Software or any Derivative Work, for free
or for payment. In particular, this license does not permit uploading either
to GitHub, GitLab, Bitbucket, another repository, a package registry, a website,
or a file-sharing service; publishing an original or modified fork; sending
source or a ZIP archive to another person; or incorporating the Software into
a product, installer, image, or project that You distribute.

Password protection, a private repository, attribution, an unchanged license,
or the noncommercial purpose of a recipient does not create permission to
Distribute. Recipients cannot obtain rights through You. Refer interested
people to the Copyright Holder's authorized source instead of sending copies.
Section 10 governs independently existing platform and other rights.

4. No commercial use or third-party service

You must not engage in Commercial Use without separate written permission.
You must not make the Software or a Derivative Work available for a Third
Party to operate, or provide its functionality to a Third Party through SaaS,
an API, managed hosting, remote access, a shared account, a hosted interface,
or any comparable arrangement. This service restriction applies even when no
copy is transferred and no fee is charged. You must not operate it on behalf
of another person or organization. These are express conditions of the rights
granted here, not a claim that all remote access is legally distribution.

