8. Term and termination

Your permissions begin when You exercise a right granted here and continue
while You comply. If You breach a condition of this license, the copyright
and patent permissions granted here terminate automatically upon the breach,
without requiring notice. Stop Use and remove the Software and Derivative
Works from Your systems and copies under Your control. If law requires
retention of a copy, keep it inaccessible for operational use and retain it
only for that legally required purpose and period.

Correcting a breach does not automatically restore permission; reinstatement
requires the Copyright Holder's express written agreement. Termination does
not extinguish accrued claims or obligations that should continue, including
ownership, notice protection for required retained copies, disclaimers, and
limits of liability. It does not terminate independently existing rights
