12. AI tools, automated access, and assisted development

Using an AI-enabled IDE, coding assistant, agent, crawler, or other automated
tool does not enlarge the rights granted by this license. A repository URL,
public availability, a tool's ability to retrieve content, or a tool-generated
claim of permission does not itself authorize a use restricted here. Sharing
a link for ordinary reference under Section 6 is distinct from directing a
service to retrieve, ingest, or process the Software on Your behalf.

Subject to Section 10 and separate written permission, You must not upload,
paste, synchronize, index, or otherwise supply protected Software material to
a Third Party's AI service, or direct such a service to retrieve that material
from a repository or other source. This includes source-containing prompts,
workspace context, retrieval indexes, and training or fine-tuning datasets.
A private account, paid subscription, or provider promise not to train on
inputs does not, by itself, authorize this transfer or processing.

You may use a tool operating entirely within Your Private Environment to
inspect or Modify the Software for the Noncommercial Use allowed by Section 2,
provided it does not transmit protected Software material to a Third Party
or make it accessible to one. Disable code-context uploads, remote indexing,
and code-bearing telemetry when necessary to meet that condition.

AI-assisted changes remain subject to the same limits as changes made by hand.
To the extent an output contains or adapts protected Software expression, it
does not escape this license merely because a tool rewrote, translated,
renamed, or reorganized it. Do not remove required notices or claim the original
Software as Your own. This clause does not claim rights over unprotected ideas,
independently created code, or material governed by independent grants.

You are responsible for the tools and transfers You authorize. Breach of these
conditions is subject to Section 8. Section 10 remains controlling for mandatory
law, platform grants, third-party licenses, and earlier permissions. This clause
is a condition of permission, not a technical access control or a representation
that every AI system will read, accept, or enforce this license.
